* bounce_models.lib - subcircuits for the GND/VCC bounce model (LTspice)
*
* DRV: linear driver model. Pull-up and pull-down are resistors controlled by IN (0..1 V).
*   x = ACT*V(IN) ; G_up = EN*x/RON ; G_dn = EN*(1-x)/RON ; plus 1/ROFF leakage on both.
*   EN=0  -> output disabled (Hi-Z), EN=1 ACT=0 -> output held low (quiet line),
*   EN=1 ACT=1 -> output follows IN with Thevenin resistance RON and a linear ramp.
*   Supply current (incl. crowbar current during the edge) flows through VCCD / GNDD.
.subckt DRV VCCD GNDD IN OUT EN=1 ACT=1 RON=11 ROFF=1Meg
BUP VCCD OUT I=V(VCCD,OUT)*({EN*ACT/RON}*V(IN)+{1/ROFF})
BDN OUT GNDD I=V(OUT,GNDD)*({EN/RON}-{EN*ACT/RON}*V(IN)+{1/ROFF})
.ends DRV
*
* TL: lossless transmission line, both ends referenced to board GND (node 0)
.subckt TL A B ZL=50 TDL=600p
T1 A 0 B 0 Zo={ZL} Td={TDL}
.ends TL
